  {
   "text": "Theileriosis (\"January Disease\")",
   "entry": "B1",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "High fever, swollen lymph nodes (especially near the ear/jaw), laboured breathing, discharge from eyes/nose, loss of appetite, rapid decline",
   "entry": "B1",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Anaplasmosis (\"Gallsickness\")",
   "entry": "B2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fever, pale or yellowish gums/mucous membranes (anaemia, jaundice), weakness, reduced appetite, sometimes dark urine",
   "entry": "B2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Babesiosis (\"Redwater\")",
   "entry": "B3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Mombe iri kuita weti tsvuku",
   "entry": "B3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "my cow is passing red urine",
   "entry": "B3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Inkomo ichama umchamo obomvu",
   "entry": "B3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fever, red-brown/\"redwater\" urine (blood in urine), anaemia, weakness, loss of appetite",
   "entry": "B3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Heartwater (Cowdriosis)",
   "entry": "B4",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "High fever, nervous signs (circling, muscle tremors, pushing head against objects, aggression or anxious behaviour), can progress rapidly to death — mortality up to 90% in susceptible animals if untreated",
   "entry": "B4",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "General tick control guidance (applies across B1–B4)",
   "entry": "B5",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Newcastle Disease (ND)",
   "entry": "C1",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Variable, but commonly: respiratory distress (gasping, coughing), greenish watery diarrhea, drop in egg production and/or thin-shelled misshapen eggs, and in later stages nervous signs (twisted neck/head, paralysis, tremors). Sudden deaths with few warning signs are common in unvaccinated flocks",
   "entry": "C1",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Infectious Bronchitis (IB)",
   "entry": "C2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Huku dziri kunetseka kufema",
   "entry": "C2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "my chickens are having difficulty breathing",
   "entry": "C2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Izinkukhu ezithwala nzima ukuphefumula",
   "entry": "C2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Coughing, sneezing, nasal discharge, watery eyes, reduced egg production, and in laying birds, misshapen or poor-quality eggshells. Generally lower mortality than ND but can be severe in young chicks",
   "entry": "C2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Coccidiosis",
   "entry": "C3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "chickens with bloody diarrhea",
   "entry": "C3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Bloody or watery diarrhea, ruffled feathers, lethargy, pale comb/wattles (anemia), reduced growth in young birds, huddling. Birds under 10-14 days old are generally not yet susceptible; risk rises as chicks start actively pecking at litter",
   "entry": "C3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Fowl Typhoid / Pullorum Disease",
   "entry": "C4",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "In young chicks: diarrhea, weakness, high mortality. In adult birds (fowl typhoid specifically): depression, pale comb, reduced appetite, greenish-yellow diarrhea, sudden deaths",
   "entry": "C4",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "General smallholder poultry biosecurity (applies across C1–C4)",
   "entry": "C5",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Gastrointestinal Parasites (Haemonchus, Eimeria)",
   "entry": "E1",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Heartwater in Goats and Sheep",
   "entry": "E2",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "Peste des Petits Ruminants (PPR) — Regional Awareness",
   "entry": "E3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "goat and sheep disease",
   "entry": "E3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "high fever, discharge from eyes/nose, mouth sores/erosions, diarrhea, pneumonia (coughing) — sudden death is possible in young kids especially",
   "entry": "E3",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
   "text": "General smallholder goat/sheep husbandry (applies across E1–E3)",
   "entry": "E4",
   "source": "farm_book"
  },
  {
